#
# THE FROZEN libpurrdf C-ABI EXPORTED-PROTOTYPE LIST.
#
# `abi-version` is the triple `purrdf_abi_version` reports; every line after it
# is one canonicalized `extern "C"` prototype from the committed
# `include/purrdf.h`, sorted. `tests/abi_signatures.rs` compares this file
# against the header on every `cargo test`.
#
# Editing a prototype here without moving `abi-version` (or the reverse) fails
# that test on purpose: a mid-list parameter insertion, a retype, a reorder, or
# a removal breaks every host compiled against the previous header, and
# `purrdf_abi_version` is the only thing that can warn them. Pre-1.0 such a
# change bumps `PURRDF_ABI_MINOR` — see `docs/book/src/project/releases.md`,
# "Pre-1.0 semver policy", and the doc comment on `PURRDF_ABI_MAJOR`.
#
# Regenerate by running `cargo test -p purrdf-capi --test abi_signatures` and
# pasting the ACTUAL block it prints. Never hand-tune a single line.

abi-version 0.7.0
